<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>ISO 20022</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Messages</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">ISO 20022</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>ISO 20022</strong> is the open international standard for financial messaging, defining XML-based message types — <strong>pacs, pain, camt</strong> and others — with rich, structured data models. In payments it replaces the legacy SWIFT MT format, and from <strong>15 November 2026</strong> its postal addresses must be fully structured or hybrid in newly initiated cross-border payments.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How ISO 20022 works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>Usage guidelines profile the standard for each channel: CBPR+ for cross-border correspondent banking, HVPS+ for RTGS systems, IP+ for instant payments, and the EPC rulebooks for SEPA. The address rules those schemes enforce are consolidated in ioNova’s <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">structured address mandate guide</a>.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §10.7 (Table 25 — implementation frameworks).</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
